1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,000
I've been on a date just once. It was back when I was in junior high.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,000
I got dressed up and went out with a boy. That was all.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,000
I ate a crepe in Harajuku. It's what everyone does.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,000
But if the person next to me was the actual real him,

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
then it would have meant the whole world to me.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Thinking back on it, I'm sure it wasn't really a date, since he was all I could think about.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000
It was sort of like we were just playing pretend.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
I can't even recall the name of the boy I went on a date with.

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000
I'm sorry. It was awful of me.

10
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
How elegant.

11
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Oh, you're up early, Noriko. Doesn't your summer vacation start today?

12
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Dad, please! Don't ruin this for me!

13
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,000
What? How am I ruining it?

14
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,000
You're ruining the elegant mood I've created in here!

15
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,000
You are such a dedicated child when it comes to acting out your little fantasies.

16
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Putting together all of your accessories and clothing seems like so much work.

17
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,000
And so what? I'm doing all of this work for myself, Kate! Just go away!

18
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,000
But come on! I want some breakfast too!

19
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:36,000
That's right. Today is a very important day for me.

20
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,000
After all, I want to make sure I look the prettiest ever in my life.

21
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,000
That's partly for him to be mesmerized.

22
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:45,000
But who am I kidding?

23
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:47,000
It's mostly for myself.

24
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Not for anyone else.

25
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
What I do is only for myself to enjoy.

26
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,000
That's how everyone should be, really.

27
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Where do you want to go?

28
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Nobody should have to find replacements.

29
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:04,000
That is, for the important people that they hold dear in their lives.

30
00:03:35,947 --> 00:03:44,807
Ah, Hanabi, are your ears pierced?

31
00:03:45,267 --> 00:03:48,627
Huh? No, they're not pierced. These are just clip-ons.

32
00:03:48,907 --> 00:03:51,007
Ah. Why aren't they pierced?

33
00:03:51,667 --> 00:03:54,427
Because I'm scared of all the pain.

34
00:03:56,167 --> 00:03:57,907
You know, that kind of turned me on.

35
00:03:58,447 --> 00:03:59,847
What are you talking about?

36
00:04:01,087 --> 00:04:02,507
Jeez, what are you looking at?

37
00:04:02,507 --> 00:04:06,307
Hey, cut it out. Give me back my phone.

38
00:04:09,127 --> 00:04:10,987
Stop it, will you? Give it back.

39
00:04:11,047 --> 00:04:12,867
Just kidding. I didn't look at it.

40
00:04:14,607 --> 00:04:15,707
Aren't you forward?

41
00:04:19,567 --> 00:04:20,047
Ow!

42
00:04:23,227 --> 00:04:26,547
Let's go to the hotel now. Come on. I'm sorry.

43
00:04:26,827 --> 00:04:27,847
I'm not going there.

44
00:04:28,187 --> 00:04:30,387
Then we'll just go to a hotel as a reward.

45
00:04:30,587 --> 00:04:32,387
Reward for what? I'm not going.

46
00:04:33,267 --> 00:04:35,247
Why does he have to mess with my head?

47
00:04:35,647 --> 00:04:37,047
You know you want to.

48
00:04:38,287 --> 00:04:38,767
Really?

49
00:04:39,667 --> 00:04:41,587
Is that all you could ever think about?

50
00:04:41,767 --> 00:04:43,867
Is your head just filled with sex 24-7?

51
00:04:44,367 --> 00:04:46,007
Yep. That's pretty much it.

52
00:04:46,407 --> 00:04:48,647
I mean, I'm a man, aren't I? So, yeah.

53
00:04:49,547 --> 00:04:50,807
That's not a good reason.

54
00:04:51,067 --> 00:04:51,527
It is.

55
00:04:51,527 --> 00:04:54,607
Don't underestimate the sex drive.

56
00:04:54,607 --> 00:04:56,107
I just want to...

57
00:04:56,107 --> 00:05:03,687
If you tease me too much, then I'm just...

58
00:05:03,687 --> 00:05:06,027
Yeah? Hello?

59
00:05:06,027 --> 00:05:08,607
Liar.

60
00:05:08,607 --> 00:05:08,907
What do you say?

61
00:05:09,167 --> 00:05:11,667
You said we could take it slow and get to know each other.

62
00:05:11,807 --> 00:05:12,567
Yeah, I'll be right there.

63
00:05:13,467 --> 00:05:13,747
Sorry.

64
00:05:14,167 --> 00:05:15,327
I'm going to split now.

65
00:05:17,447 --> 00:05:18,447
Who was that?

66
00:05:18,447 --> 00:05:21,647
A girl who's going to let me do her.

67
00:05:22,387 --> 00:05:22,907
See ya.

68
00:05:23,287 --> 00:05:23,627
Hey!

69
00:05:24,347 --> 00:05:25,187
Hold on!

70
00:05:25,187 --> 00:05:31,067
You're stretching my shirt.

71
00:05:31,747 --> 00:05:32,947
I'm so sorry.

72
00:05:34,247 --> 00:05:35,847
Uh, are you sure about this?

73
00:05:36,287 --> 00:05:38,467
I mean, it's the movie I want to see.

74
00:05:38,867 --> 00:05:40,327
You might think it's too boring.

75
00:05:40,827 --> 00:05:41,027
Hmm.

76
00:05:41,027 --> 00:05:43,307
But you'll like it.

77
00:05:43,827 --> 00:05:44,807
Come on, let's go.

78
00:05:47,827 --> 00:05:48,307
I...

79
00:05:48,307 --> 00:05:50,347
I want to hold his hand.

80
00:05:51,247 --> 00:05:52,867
But for now...

81
00:05:52,867 --> 00:05:53,567
Hold on!

82
00:05:53,827 --> 00:05:54,807
Yeah, sure. Okay.

83
00:05:56,107 --> 00:05:58,627
All you need to do is turn and look at me.

84
00:05:59,267 --> 00:06:00,367
That's all I need.

85
00:06:01,047 --> 00:06:02,487
I am truly happy.

86
00:06:09,407 --> 00:06:10,867
There's nobody else in here.

87
00:06:11,247 --> 00:06:11,847
Uh, yeah.

88
00:06:12,047 --> 00:06:13,027
I guess there's not.

89
00:06:13,727 --> 00:06:14,287
What now?

90
00:06:14,667 --> 00:06:16,307
I'm the one who wanted to see this.

91
00:06:16,547 --> 00:06:18,507
But I can't seem to pay attention at all.

92
00:06:19,047 --> 00:06:22,967
It's because it's just really Mookie and I here all alone together.

93
00:06:23,487 --> 00:06:26,427
I didn't know that a theater could bring us so close.

94
00:06:26,867 --> 00:06:27,687
I've loved you.

95
00:06:28,227 --> 00:06:29,327
For all my life.

96
00:06:30,087 --> 00:06:33,927
I never knew how wonderful it is to be in love.

97
00:06:36,007 --> 00:06:36,327
Hmm.

98
00:06:38,067 --> 00:06:40,267
What about a love that never happens?

99
00:06:41,027 --> 00:06:42,267
Is it just misery?

100
00:06:42,927 --> 00:06:44,027
It's okay, though.

101
00:06:44,667 --> 00:06:46,327
I love you enough to live with that.

102
00:06:46,987 --> 00:06:47,227
Mookie?

103
00:06:47,887 --> 00:06:48,887
That's not true.

104
00:06:49,527 --> 00:06:51,847
Even if it never blossoms, love is...

105
00:06:51,847 --> 00:06:56,847
Oh, that's a lie.

106
00:06:57,967 --> 00:07:01,867
If there's not a happy ending, then I don't want it.

107
00:07:01,867 --> 00:07:06,947
That was pretty good, huh?

108
00:07:07,687 --> 00:07:08,087
Really?

109
00:07:08,587 --> 00:07:09,487
Thank goodness.

110
00:07:10,147 --> 00:07:11,487
What do you mean, thank goodness?

111
00:07:12,367 --> 00:07:14,027
Uh, I mean...

112
00:07:14,027 --> 00:07:18,447
I would have felt bad if you didn't like it, since I was the one that picked it out and everything.

113
00:07:18,927 --> 00:07:21,867
If it ended up boring, then it would have been the movie's fault.

114
00:07:22,527 --> 00:07:24,127
It's not something you should worry about.

115
00:07:24,127 --> 00:07:24,747
I...

116
00:07:24,747 --> 00:07:27,447
I love him.

117
00:07:28,907 --> 00:07:29,307
Mookie?

118
00:07:29,307 --> 00:07:29,407
Mookie?

119
00:07:30,667 --> 00:07:33,287
I wonder how he felt about what I did.

120
00:07:34,727 --> 00:07:35,207
Mookie?

121
00:07:36,667 --> 00:07:37,627
Hey, Mookie?

122
00:07:37,627 --> 00:07:43,827
Did you know, if you go to sleep holding hands, you will both have the same dream?

123
00:07:44,547 --> 00:07:49,507
I want so badly to tell him, but I can't do it.

124
00:07:51,507 --> 00:07:54,647
It's as if I'm in a dream right now.

125
00:07:55,507 --> 00:07:55,827
Mocha.

126
00:07:57,047 --> 00:07:57,927
I'm hungry.

127
00:07:58,167 --> 00:07:58,887
Let's get some food.

128
00:07:59,447 --> 00:08:00,287
Thank goodness.

129
00:08:00,667 --> 00:08:02,107
I'm still dreaming.

130
00:08:03,147 --> 00:08:03,467
Mm-hmm.

131
00:08:15,707 --> 00:08:17,247
Why did I do that?

132
00:08:17,847 --> 00:08:19,867
Why did I stop him in the first place?

133
00:08:22,047 --> 00:08:23,367
Hey, hold on!

134
00:08:25,167 --> 00:08:25,687
What?

135
00:08:26,407 --> 00:08:27,447
You let me do you?

136
00:08:28,007 --> 00:08:29,687
No, I...

137
00:08:29,687 --> 00:08:30,727
Um...

138
00:08:30,727 --> 00:08:33,887
Later.

139
00:08:35,567 --> 00:08:38,847
I chased after him like an idiot, but it didn't work.

140
00:08:39,687 --> 00:08:41,407
In the end, he just left me anyway.

141
00:08:42,407 --> 00:08:45,387
Now all I'm left with is my stubborn pride.

142
00:08:46,107 --> 00:08:46,707
That's all.

143
00:08:47,367 --> 00:08:49,207
I never got him to fall in love with me.

144
00:08:50,007 --> 00:08:51,307
Only lust over me.

145
00:08:52,027 --> 00:08:53,207
But I was fine with that.

146
00:08:54,167 --> 00:08:55,887
It's not like I can tell the difference.

147
00:08:56,947 --> 00:08:59,027
Love or lust, they all feel the same to me now.

148
00:08:59,687 --> 00:09:03,467
I want to be obsessed over her.

149
00:09:03,787 --> 00:09:05,007
I want all their desires.

150
00:09:05,387 --> 00:09:06,487
I won't give them anything.

151
00:09:06,907 --> 00:09:09,207
And I won't let them take anything from me either.

152
00:09:09,727 --> 00:09:10,847
It can't be equal.

153
00:09:11,687 --> 00:09:12,727
Please, someone.

154
00:09:13,487 --> 00:09:14,427
I don't care who.

155
00:09:14,867 --> 00:09:15,887
I just want you to...

156
00:09:15,887 --> 00:09:18,287
I want you to think I'm worth something.

157
00:09:18,287 --> 00:09:20,507
This is pathetic.

158
00:09:21,067 --> 00:09:23,087
Since when did I become this sort of woman?

159
00:09:24,087 --> 00:09:26,607
At first, I just thought...

160
00:09:26,607 --> 00:09:28,607
I wanted to be with the person I loved.

161
00:09:29,247 --> 00:09:30,287
But why, God?

162
00:09:30,587 --> 00:09:31,827
Why is it like this?

163
00:09:32,507 --> 00:09:35,647
Why does unrequited love always leave you feeling so empty?

164
00:09:35,647 --> 00:09:39,267
I want to see you.

165
00:09:39,427 --> 00:09:40,267
Let's meet.

166
00:09:42,667 --> 00:09:43,867
Is that your phone?

167
00:09:44,687 --> 00:09:45,967
You can answer it.

168
00:09:47,387 --> 00:09:48,627
Uh, no.

169
00:09:49,187 --> 00:09:49,887
It's fine.

170
00:09:50,427 --> 00:09:52,707
Please, you don't need to hold back on my account.

171
00:09:52,707 --> 00:09:54,787
What am I saying?

172
00:09:55,387 --> 00:09:56,747
This is not enough.

173
00:09:58,067 --> 00:09:59,167
Just smile.

174
00:10:00,027 --> 00:10:01,447
I had fun today, didn't I?

175
00:10:02,107 --> 00:10:03,447
Aren't I satisfied?

176
00:10:04,447 --> 00:10:06,107
So I should just smile.

177
00:10:06,667 --> 00:10:07,047
Go on.

178
00:10:08,127 --> 00:10:10,407
It tastes good, doesn't it?

179
00:10:11,807 --> 00:10:17,007
Because soon, I'll eventually realize it's nothing but a silly dream.

180
00:10:17,007 --> 00:10:20,967
I can't believe it's still muggy now.

181
00:10:21,727 --> 00:10:23,447
Thanks for staying out so late with me.

182
00:10:24,027 --> 00:10:24,927
I, um...

183
00:10:24,927 --> 00:10:26,547
That was fun, Mookie.

184
00:10:28,287 --> 00:10:28,807
Yeah?

185
00:10:29,587 --> 00:10:31,807
I'm glad I realized it halfway through.

186
00:10:32,887 --> 00:10:33,527
That's right.

187
00:10:33,927 --> 00:10:35,147
If it's not going to happen,

188
00:10:35,647 --> 00:10:37,867
then I just need to give myself good memories.

189
00:10:38,527 --> 00:10:40,487
I can recreate the perfect dream

190
00:10:40,487 --> 00:10:42,107
and just hold on to it,

191
00:10:42,347 --> 00:10:44,507
playing it back over and over again.

192
00:10:44,787 --> 00:10:45,767
I'll watch it forever.

193
00:10:46,247 --> 00:10:47,207
It'll just be mild.

194
00:10:47,227 --> 00:10:48,007
Hey, Mocha.

195
00:10:49,247 --> 00:10:50,007
What's wrong?

196
00:10:50,187 --> 00:10:50,987
Something happened?

197
00:10:51,467 --> 00:10:52,547
You're acting strange.

198
00:10:52,927 --> 00:10:54,427
Do you realize how long it's been

199
00:10:54,427 --> 00:10:56,307
since you actually looked at me today?

200
00:10:56,487 --> 00:10:58,387
I was about to make a horrible mistake

201
00:10:58,387 --> 00:10:59,427
I couldn't take back.

202
00:10:59,907 --> 00:11:02,227
If he had rejected me when our hands touched,

203
00:11:02,487 --> 00:11:03,627
I would have just died.

204
00:11:04,067 --> 00:11:05,607
I wouldn't have been able to go on.

205
00:11:06,427 --> 00:11:07,987
I can keep on living my life

206
00:11:07,987 --> 00:11:09,647
without a real love to call my own.

207
00:11:10,287 --> 00:11:10,607
Hey.

208
00:11:11,107 --> 00:11:13,147
Mookie, I had a lot of fun today.

209
00:11:13,567 --> 00:11:14,907
I'm truly thankful.

210
00:11:15,767 --> 00:11:16,867
I'll cherish this.

211
00:11:17,307 --> 00:11:19,607
This memory is forever mine.

212
00:11:22,427 --> 00:11:25,307
I can continue living in an endless dream

213
00:11:25,307 --> 00:11:26,047
that isn't real.

214
00:11:26,567 --> 00:11:28,647
I can make that come true by myself.

215
00:11:29,867 --> 00:11:30,207
And I...

216
00:11:30,887 --> 00:11:32,207
I know...

217
00:11:33,327 --> 00:11:34,207
I can...

218
00:11:34,207 --> 00:11:35,847
be happy.

219
00:11:38,227 --> 00:11:39,527
I love you.

220
00:11:41,107 --> 00:11:41,547
Mookie.

221
00:11:41,547 --> 00:11:48,267
And like that,

222
00:11:49,047 --> 00:11:52,127
the princess' kiss shatters the dream I had built up.

223
00:11:53,087 --> 00:11:55,727
And the princess finally awakes to find

224
00:11:55,727 --> 00:11:57,527
she's left in darkness.

225
00:11:58,347 --> 00:12:00,827
And the reason she doesn't cry herself hoarse

226
00:12:00,827 --> 00:12:03,207
is because she has not yet learned

227
00:12:03,207 --> 00:12:05,707
sadness nor happiness.

228
00:12:05,707 --> 00:12:08,207
I'm tired.

229
00:12:10,387 --> 00:12:12,207
There's nobody I want to see.

230
00:12:12,847 --> 00:12:13,847
I hate men.

231
00:12:14,587 --> 00:12:15,807
I can't see Sanai.

232
00:12:16,867 --> 00:12:17,527
A friend.

233
00:12:18,687 --> 00:12:20,287
I don't have any friends.

234
00:12:21,747 --> 00:12:22,307
Oh well.

235
00:12:23,047 --> 00:12:25,087
Sometimes I do feel like just being alone.

236
00:12:25,087 --> 00:12:31,807
It's been a while

237
00:12:31,807 --> 00:12:34,167
since I've been in here.

238
00:12:34,827 --> 00:12:36,267
When was the last time?

239
00:12:37,367 --> 00:12:38,607
It smells nice.

240
00:12:39,887 --> 00:12:40,187
Mocha,

241
00:12:40,627 --> 00:12:42,027
sorry you didn't have fun.

242
00:12:42,687 --> 00:12:43,867
I did have fun.

243
00:12:44,727 --> 00:12:45,547
You're lying.

244
00:12:46,207 --> 00:12:47,147
I'm not lying.

245
00:12:47,147 --> 00:12:49,067
But it was lacking

246
00:12:49,067 --> 00:12:50,307
as much as it was fun,

247
00:12:50,547 --> 00:12:51,507
I guess you could say.

248
00:12:52,887 --> 00:12:54,047
I wonder why.

249
00:12:54,727 --> 00:12:56,147
I pretend I don't know,

250
00:12:56,467 --> 00:12:57,327
even though I do.

251
00:12:58,027 --> 00:12:58,867
You wanna know?

252
00:12:59,447 --> 00:13:00,427
I don't know.

253
00:13:00,907 --> 00:13:01,347
I see.

254
00:13:02,227 --> 00:13:02,727
I know.

255
00:13:03,807 --> 00:13:05,487
I've known for a while now.

256
00:13:10,427 --> 00:13:11,347
Well then,

257
00:13:11,707 --> 00:13:12,607
good night, Noriko.

258
00:13:13,267 --> 00:13:13,707
Okay.

259
00:13:14,227 --> 00:13:15,027
Good night, Mama.

260
00:13:15,027 --> 00:13:18,887
Dear perfect god in all of heaven,

261
00:13:19,447 --> 00:13:21,027
please let Mookie and I

262
00:13:21,027 --> 00:13:24,787
be married and live in Versailles one day.

263
00:13:25,827 --> 00:13:27,467
I don't wanna go live there.

264
00:13:27,707 --> 00:13:29,247
I'd rather be in Himeji Castle.

265
00:13:30,407 --> 00:13:32,407
A shogun is way better than a prince.

266
00:13:32,627 --> 00:13:33,927
I wish I could grow a mustache.

267
00:13:35,007 --> 00:13:36,447
You want me to be the prince

268
00:13:36,447 --> 00:13:37,447
in this play of yours?

269
00:13:37,747 --> 00:13:38,787
Not interested.

270
00:13:39,207 --> 00:13:40,467
I'm fine being a tree.

271
00:13:41,087 --> 00:13:42,507
Trees are always nice and big.

272
00:13:42,687 --> 00:13:43,947
I'd like to go to Yakushima.

273
00:13:45,027 --> 00:13:45,587
No way!

274
00:13:45,667 --> 00:13:47,567
You and I are going to England and France

275
00:13:47,567 --> 00:13:48,287
for our honeymoon,

276
